==English==

{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Machette_kos.pg.jpg|thumb|right|250px|a machete]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/məˈʃɛ.ti/}}
* {{audio|En-us-ncalif-machete.ogg|Audio (US, Northern California)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|es|en}} {{term|machete|lang=es}}, diminutive of {{term|macho|lang=es||sledgehammer}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|mattea|lang=la}}, cognate with Old French {{term|machier|lang=fro}}, French {{term|massue|lang=fr}}, English {{term|mace|lang=fr}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sword]]-like [[tool]] used for [[cut]]ting large [[plant]]s with a [[chop]]ping motion. A machete's blade is usually 50 to 65 centimeters ([[cm]]) long, and up to three millimeters ([[mm]]) thick.

====Synonyms====
* [[bolo]]

